## 14. End-to-end experience requirements

### Navigation and route behavior

- **UX-1:** The primary navigation contains Overview, Skill Library, Sources, Skill Studio, Insights, and Settings, with active-page indication and skill count where available.
- **UX-2:** The brand returns to Overview. Quick search, Explore/Library, featured-skill, create-skill, edit-skill, and back-to-library links lead to the expected pages.
- **UX-3:** Keep `/marketplace` as a compatibility redirect to `/library`; unknown routes show a recovery link instead of a blank screen.
- **UX-4:** The mobile menu opens and closes accessibly, closes after navigation, and has a visible/keyboard-operable close mechanism.
- **UX-5:** Do not advertise a keyboard shortcut unless it works. The current library displays `⌘ K`, but the frontend does not implement a key handler; either implement the shortcut (with platform-aware modifier and focus behavior) or remove the hint.

### Loading, empty, error, and success states

- **UX-6:** Distinguish initial loading from an empty catalog, no search results, missing record, API failure, and permission failure.
- **UX-7:** Provide retry actions for recoverable reads and explain whether a write succeeded before navigation or clearing user input.
- **UX-8:** Do not show an indefinite spinner when a requested skill is missing. Resolve `404` to the not-found state and provide a path back to the library.
- **UX-9:** Keep errors close to the operation that failed and do not show stale data as current without labeling it.
- **UX-10:** A header “API connected” indicator must represent a verified health check, not merely the presence of an API URL; otherwise label it “API configured.”

### Skill discovery and browsing

- **UX-11:** Debounce text search and communicate when results are being refreshed.
- **UX-12:** Define whether multiple selected topics use AND or OR semantics; display all available facet options independently of the currently narrowed results if users are expected to broaden a search.
- **UX-13:** Keep the matching count, displayed cards, and backend pagination totals consistent. The current API adapter always requests page 1 with page size 100; larger catalogs require pagination or a documented product cap.
- **UX-14:** Grid/list switching changes presentation only; do not discard search, sort, source, or topic state.
- **UX-15:** A card must have one clear primary navigation action. Any secondary action (including the current ellipsis control) must perform a defined task or be removed.

### Skill detail, copy, and export

- **UX-16:** Clipboard permission or browser errors must produce visible feedback and must not leave the user assuming content was copied.
- **UX-17:** ZIP export must preserve the full instruction content and the agreed metadata schema; surface generation/download errors.
- **UX-18:** Show an external repository link only when the skill has a real, valid repository URL. A local/workspace origin must not be formatted as a GitHub owner/repository path.
- **UX-19:** Clearly distinguish sample metrics, user-authored skills, imported/source-backed skills, and unavailable metadata.

### Skill authoring

- **UX-20:** Define a canonical name/slug rule, uniqueness scope, allowed characters, and collision behavior. Validation must be shown at the field or form level.
- **UX-21:** Define which fields users may edit. In the current frontend, new skills receive defaults for language (`Markdown`), platforms (`Claude Code`, `Cursor`), source (`local/skillcatalog`), stars/downloads (`0`), and version (`1.0.0`); the form does not ask for these values.
- **UX-22:** State whether Markdown instructions are required and any maximum size. The current UI requires only name and description.
- **UX-23:** If draft autosave is promised, persist it across route changes/reloads with clear recovery and discard behavior. The current editor says “Draft autosaves in this session,” but its fields are only component state and are not actually autosaved.
- **UX-24:** Import must report unreadable/unsupported files and preserve the current draft if import fails. The current UI accepts `.md`, `.txt`, and `.skill`.
- **UX-25:** The preview must either render sanitized Markdown or be explicitly described as a plain-text preview. The current editor displays raw text, not rendered Markdown.
- **UX-26:** Formatting controls must apply predictable Markdown at the cursor/selection and remain usable with keyboard and assistive technology.
- **UX-27:** On successful save, return the canonical backend record and route to its detail page. On failure, keep the entered values and show a retryable error.

### Sources and synchronization

- **UX-28:** Identify which source types are supported and validate URLs before save. The current create form only captures a name and URL and defaults the type to `github_repo`; the seed source is an `awesome_list`.
- **UX-29:** Communicate that manual sync may be asynchronous. Show the latest actual job state and completion time; poll or refresh until a queued/running job reaches a terminal state.
- **UX-30:** Provide confirmation for destructive source removal and clearly explain what happens to skills obtained from that source.
- **UX-31:** Disable duplicate submissions while operations are running and show operation-specific progress/success/error feedback.

### Insights and settings

- **UX-32:** Explain metric definitions and source attribution; do not label summed demo values as community-wide totals.
- **UX-33:** Use a real data-refresh timestamp instead of a hard-coded “Updated just now” label.
- **UX-34:** Keep unsupported server-provided schedule values visible or provide a clear validation response rather than silently substituting a default.
- **UX-35:** Provide clear token submission outcomes. Token validation and storage are backend responsibilities; a successful settings write alone must not imply the token has been validated unless the API confirms it.
- **UX-36:** Keep secrets out of browser persistence, URL parameters, client logs, and error messages. Clear the field after any submission attempt; if the operation fails, require re-entry before retry.

### Responsive design and accessibility

- **UX-37:** Preserve the current desktop/sidebar, tablet, and mobile layouts across overview, library, detail, editor, sources, dashboard, and settings.
- **UX-38:** All navigation, form inputs, filters, toggles, dialogs, copy/export actions, and editor tools must be keyboard operable with visible focus and accessible names.
- **UX-39:** Announce loading, result updates, validation errors, save outcomes, and sync status to assistive technology without relying on color alone.
- **UX-40:** Support narrow screens without horizontal overflow; on mobile, stack the editor panes and keep important actions reachable.

## 15. Current frontend limitations to carry into rebuild planning

These are observed gaps or caveats, not additional features already delivered:

1. **No backend in this project:** API mode is a client adapter contract. Persistence, authentication, authorization, scheduled work, and repository processing must be implemented and verified separately.
2. **No authentication or ownership UI:** All edit, source, and settings controls are exposed without role checks; the backend must enforce the chosen access model.
3. **No actual quick-search shortcut:** The UI shows a `⌘ K` hint, but no keyboard listener focuses search.
4. **No actual draft autosave:** The editor copy claims session autosave, but there is no persistence mechanism for drafts.
5. **Not-found detail can spin indefinitely:** `getSkill` can return `null` for 404, while the detail component treats every null skill as still loading.
6. **Library result ceiling:** The API client requests the first 100 skills only; no next-page control or result-total handling exists.
7. **Source sync is not monitored:** The source screen sends one sync request and reloads sources. It does not poll job status, show logs, or verify completion.
8. **Demo sync is simulated:** In demo mode, sync only changes `last_synced_at`; it does not contact a repository or import content.
9. **Some user feedback is incomplete:** Clipboard and ZIP operations do not have complete failure handling; source sync/remove do not have a dedicated in-progress indicator.
10. **Source provenance needs a model:** A locally created skill defaults to `local/skillcatalog`, but detail rendering treats every non-demo source as a GitHub repository slug.
11. **Dashboard data is derived client-side:** Metrics and topic counts are computed from the loaded skills/sources; “Updated just now” is static, not a backend timestamp.
12. **Settings do not validate GitHub credentials in the UI:** The token is posted to the backend when configured; demo mode does not store it. The frontend has no explicit token-validation response flow. It clears the field after a successful save but retains it after a failed save; the target requirement is to clear after every submission attempt and ask for re-entry on retry.
13. **Editor preview is plain text:** It is not a rendered Markdown preview, and its frontmatter indicator checks delimiters only rather than parsing/validating fields.
14. **Demo data is local and synthetic:** Demo skills and their stars/downloads are illustrative. Demo edits persist only in browser storage and are not shared across users.
15. **No skill deletion flow:** Skills can be created and edited; the current detail UI has no delete action, even though deletion may be considered for a later product release.
16. **The card overflow control has no action:** Either define a meaningful menu (for example, copy link) or omit the control from a rebuild.

The rebuild should either implement a gap as an explicit requirement or intentionally exclude it and remove misleading labels/controls. It should not silently reproduce incomplete behavior as if it were finished.

## 16. Expanded acceptance checklist

- [ ] Every route and navigation action in Section 13 works, including the legacy redirect and unknown-route recovery.
- [ ] Desktop, tablet, and mobile navigation/layouts work without loss of content or controls.
- [ ] Keyboard shortcuts are implemented if shown; all interactive controls have visible keyboard focus.
- [ ] Skill list search/filter/sort/count behavior agrees with API results and pagination.
- [ ] Search, source, tag, sort, and view state behave consistently when users change filters or open/return from details.
- [ ] Missing skills show not-found; API errors offer a useful recovery action rather than indefinite loading.
- [ ] Copy/export success and failure states are clear; exports contain valid content and metadata.
- [ ] Authoring validation covers name, description, content policy, tags, size, and uniqueness; imported files fail safely.
- [ ] Draft persistence behavior matches the UI promise.
- [ ] A successful create/update persists centrally and is visible after reload; failed writes preserve the draft.
- [ ] Source CRUD, destructive confirmation, source provenance, asynchronous sync progress, and terminal sync outcomes are tested.
- [ ] Dashboard values and timestamps are authoritative or clearly labeled as unavailable/sample.
- [ ] Settings persist and token validation is explicit; no secrets are returned, stored client-side, or leaked in logs.
- [ ] API mode failures never masquerade as demo success; demo-only behavior is clearly labeled.
- [ ] Accessibility checks include keyboard-only operation, accessible naming, status announcements, and responsive zoom/layout.
